guamp: NMB_SHADOW_DIFF merges a shadowed texture's writes back as the bytes they changed (bridge 0063)

HakiOS (analisi/hakios-confronto-20261107.md, idea 1; idea only, no code taken: its plug-in has no licence) cured "black bands moving
from frame to frame" by writing a surface's shadow back only where its bytes differ from the copy the shadow started from. In
metal2vulkan the copies are GPU commands ordered by the tracker, so the encode-time race they had cannot happen inside one process;
what a copy back can still undo is a write the encoder does not order (another process's work on the same IOSurface, a CPU write
racing the GPU): the copy back sets the whole written area to what the copy in saw. The runtime already merges a command that writes
a texture two ways (shadow_merge.rs: kept copy, changed copy, current bytes, one dispatch taking the changed bytes). NMB_SHADOW_DIFF
(boot line through guamp-m2v-env, 0019) sends writes through a mergeable shadow of bytes down that path: =1 every write, =2 only a
write the command does not bound (no scissor bound, a copy back of the whole texture); unset/0 as before. A pass that replaces every
texel (cleared attachment) still copies back. Cost: a scratch of three copies of the texture and a dispatch instead of one copy back
(~4x the copy traffic of a 750x1666 framebuffer: diagnostic, default off). Pairs with 0051/0057: NMB_PARTIAL_IN=0 copies in whole,
NMB_SHADOW_DIFF=1 also copies in whole (a merge compares every byte).
Applies after bridge 0051/0057 (shadow.rs ShadowSync). Host: metal2vulkan-runtime --lib 891 passed (new test shadow diff setting).

